{"subject": "spanish","level": "ks3","topic_display": "Family Members","topic_slug": "family-members","theme": "languages-stamps","adventure_n": 1,"title": "Parents & Siblings","emoji": "👨‍👩‍👧","welcome_lead": "Madre, padre, hermano, hermana.","meta_desc": "KS3 Spanish: family vocab — parents and siblings.","final_note": "Family vocabulary unlocks describing yourself.","concepts": [{"term": "La madre","def": "The mother."},{"term": "El padre","def": "The father."},{"term": "Mama","def": "Mum."},{"term": "Papa","def": "Dad."},{"term": "El hermano","def": "The brother."},{"term": "La hermana","def": "The sister."}],"walkthroughs": [{"tag": "Two","h2": "El & La","body_html": "<p>Spanish has just two genders: <strong>el</strong> (masculine), <strong>la</strong> (feminine). 'El padre', 'la madre'. Most nouns ending in -o are masculine, -a are feminine.</p>"},{"tag": "Sibs","h2": "Brothers & Sisters","body_html": "<p><strong>El hermano</strong> = brother. <strong>La hermana</strong> = sister. Plurals add -s: <strong>los hermanos</strong>, <strong>las hermanas</strong>.</p>"},{"tag": "Have","h2": "Saying You Have","body_html": "<p><strong>Tengo</strong> = I have. 'Tengo un hermano y dos hermanas' = 'I have one brother and two sisters'. <strong>Un/una</strong> = a/an.</p>"}],"mcqs": [{"q": "What is 'la hermana'?","options": [["Brother",false],["Sister",true],["Mother",false],["Aunt",false]]},{"q": "Spanish 'el' is for which gender?","options": [["Feminine",false],["Masculine",true],["Neuter",false],["Plural",false]]},{"q": "How do you describe weather during a past holiday: 'It was sunny'?","options": [["Preterite - 'Hizo sol' (suggests a completed event).",0],["Imperfect - 'Hacía sol' (descriptive ongoing state).",1],["Present - 'Hace sol'.",0],["Infinitive.",0]]},{"q": "Which mood follows 'Espero que' (I hope that)?","options": [["Present - 'Hace sol'.",0],["Subjunctive - 'Espero que tengas éxito'.",1],["Indicative - 'Espero que tienes éxito'.",0],["Infinitive.",0]]},{"q": "How do you say 'I love films' in Spanish?","options": [["Infinitive.",0],["Yo amo películas.",0],["Me encantan las películas.",1],["Me encanta las películas.",0]]},{"q": "Which of these is the best definition of “La madre”?","options": [["The mother.",1],["The sister.",0],["The father.",0],["Mum.",0]]},{"q": "Which of these is the best definition of “El hermano”?","options": [["The mother.",0],["The brother.",1],["Dad.",0],["Mum.",0]]},{"q": "Which of these is the best definition of “Mama”?","options": [["Mum.",1],["Dad.",0],["The mother.",0],["The sister.",0]]},{"q": "Which of these is the best definition of “Papa”?","options": [["The father.",0],["Dad.",1],["The mother.",0],["The sister.",0]]},{"q": "Which of these is the best definition of “La hermana”?","options": [["Dad.",0],["The sister.",1],["Mum.",0],["The mother.",0]]},{"q": "Which of these is the best definition of “El padre”?","options": [["Mum.",0],["The sister.",0],["The father.",1],["Dad.",0]]},{"q": "How many Spanish genders for 'the'?","options": [["2",1],["4",0],["1",0],["3",0]]}],"numericals": [{"q": "How many Spanish genders for 'the'?","options": [1,2,3,4],"answer": 2}],"free_texts": [{"q": "What is Spanish for brother (drop article)? (lowercase ASCII)","answer": "hermano"}],"mcqs_expanded": true,"sequence": [{"term": "El bisabuelo","def": "Great-grandfather — three generations above you"},{"term": "El abuelo","def": "Grandfather — two generations above you"},{"term": "El padre","def": "Father — one generation above you"},{"term": "Yo","def": "You — the centre of the family tree"},{"term": "El hijo","def": "Son — one generation below you"},{"term": "El nieto","def": "Grandson — two generations below you"}]}